  "result": "Methanoculleus chikugoensis sp. nov., a novel methanogenic archaeon isolated from paddy field soil in Japan, and DNA-DNA hybridization among Methanoculleus species. (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11594593/)\nciteturn30search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago;   * DOI: 10.1099/00207713-51-5-1663 ... The strain was able to use H2/CO2, 2-propanol/CO2, formate, 2-butanol/CO2 and cyclopentanol/CO2 as substrates for methanogenesis, but did not utilize acetate, ethanol, methanol or methylamines.\n# Methanoculleus chikugoensis sp. nov., a novel methanogenic archaeon isolated from paddy field soil in Japan, and DNA-DNA hybridization among Methanoculleus species.\n\nInternational journal of systematic and evolutionary microbiology\n\nPMID: 11594593\n\nPublication date: 2001 Sep\n\nPublication status: ppublish\n\nJournal abbreviation: Int J Syst Evol Microbiol\n\nJournal country: England\n\nJournal NLM unique ID: 100899600\n\nJournal linking ISSN: 1466-5026\n\nISSN: 1466-5026\n\nVolume: 51\n\nIssue: Pt 5\n\nPages: 1663-1669\n\n## Identifiers\n\n  * DOI: 10.1099/00207713-51-5-1663\n\n## Authors\n\n  * D Dianou\n  * T Miyaki\n  * S Asakawa\n  * H Morii\n  * K Nagaoka\n  * H Oyaizu\n  * S Matsumoto\n\n## Languages\n\n  * eng\n\n## Publication types\n\n  * Journal Article\n  * Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't\n\n## Abstract\n\nA strictly anaerobic, irregularly coccoid, methanogenic archaeon, strain MG62T (= JCM 10825T = DSM 13459T), was isolated from paddy field soil in Chikugo, Fukuoka, Japan. The cells stained gram-negative, were 1.0-2.0 microm in diameter, were lysed by SDS and hypotonic solutions and were flagellated. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nammonium carbonate (CHEBI:229630) (https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/CHEBI%3A229630)\nciteturn30search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Baker's ammonia  | ChEBI ... carbonic acid ammonium salt (1:2)  | ChEBI\n\n## CHEBI:229630 - ammonium carbonate\n\nImage: Default Structure\n\nTake structure to advanced search\n\nChEBI ID  | CHEBI:229630\nChEBI Name  | ammonium carbonate\nStars  | \nDefinition  | An ammonium salt that is the diammonium salt of carbonic acid.\nLast Modified  | 6 March 2024\nSubmitter  | ntejera\n\nFormula  | CO3.2H4N\nNet Charge  | 0\nAverage Mass  | 96.086\nMonoisotopic Mass  | 96.05349\nSMILES  | O=C([O-])[O-].[NH4+].[NH4+]\nInChI  | InChI=1S/CH2O3.2H3N/c2-1(3)4;;/h(H2,2,3,4);2*1H3\nInChIKey  | PRKQVKDSMLBJBJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N\n\nChemical Roles:  | raising agent  A food additive which liberates gas so as to increase the volume of a dough or batter, resulting in a lighter and softer finished product.food acidity regulator  A food additive that is used to change or otherwise control the acidity or alkalinity of foods. They may be acids, bases, neutralising agents or buffering agents.\nBiological Roles:  | raising agent  A food additive which liberates gas so as to increase the volume of a dough or batter, resulting in a lighter and softer finished product.food acidity regulator  A food additive that is used to change or otherwise control the acidity or alkalinity of foods. They may be acids, bases, neutralising agents or buffering agents.\nApplications:  | raising agent  A food additive which liberates gas so as to increase the volume of a dough or batter, resulting in a lighter and softer finished product.food acidity regulator  A food additive that is used to change or otherwise control the acidity or alkalinity of foods. They may be acids, bases, neutralising agents or buffering agents.\n\nChEBI Ontology\n---\n\nText\n\nTree View\n\nGraph View\n\nOutgoing Relation(s)\nammonium carbonate (CHEBI:229630) has role food acidity regulator (CHEBI:64049)\nammonium carbonate (CHEBI:229630) has role raising agent (CHEBI:77971)\nammonium carbonate (CHEBI:229630) is a ammonium salt (CHEBI:47704)\nammonium carbonate (CHEBI:229630) is a carbonate salt (CHEBI:46721)\n\nIUPAC Name \n---\ndiammonium carbonate\n\nSynonym s 